    "reason": "The only evidence is the v2.0.0 CRD file for ClusterUsage [ev-067b435b635b], and its excerpt is empty (\"---\"). It shows the CRD was added and nothing more. The line \"Install or update CRDs before upgrading if you manage them separately\" is a generic hint attached to the computed diff, not an upstream statement that anything fails or that a step is mandatory, so migration-required (action-required, high) is not supported. Because no evidence says what happens if the CRD is missing, \"none\" would also be a guess. Deciding this needs release notes or an upgrade guide that say whether Crossplane or the upgrade fails when separately managed CRDs leave out clusterusages.protection.crossplane.io.",
